@startuml
!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title Event-driven Payment Processing — Synthetic HLD
actor "Merchant" as Merchant
package "Payment Platform" {
 component "Merchant API" as API
 component "Payment Orchestrator" as Orch
 component "Callback Ingress" as Callback
 component "Payment State Consumer" as Consumer
 component "Transactional Outbox / CDC" as Relay
 component "Recovery Worker" as Recovery
 component "Merchant Webhook Delivery" as Webhook
 component "Reconciliation" as Recon
 database "Payment State + Inbox + Outbox" as DB
 database "Payment Ledger / Audit" as Ledger
 queue "Kafka Topics" as Kafka
}
component "Processor Adapter" as Adapter
cloud "External Payment Provider" as Provider
Merchant --> API : Create intent / status
API --> Orch : Validated request
Orch --> DB : Atomic state + outbox
Relay --> DB : Read committed outbox
Relay --> Kafka : Publish (at least once)
Kafka --> Consumer : Payment events
Consumer --> DB : Inbox dedupe + guarded state update + outbox
Consumer --> Adapter : Submit only if safe
Adapter --> Provider : Provider command / inquiry
Provider ..> Callback : Signed status callback
Callback --> DB : Verify + persist ingress
Kafka --> Webhook : Confirmed business outcome
Webhook ..> Merchant : Retry merchant notification
Recovery ..> Provider : Status enquiry for UNKNOWN
Recovery --> DB : Guarded result update + outbox
Recon ..> Provider : Reconcile external records
Recon --> Ledger : Controlled financial updates
note bottom of Kafka
Kafka can redeliver. No global order.
Never replay unknown financial instructions blindly.
end note
@enduml